From: buntOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: mt6375-charger: tell the fuel gauge how a charge goes

The fuel gauge reports the status of the battery, and it cannot see a
charge end under the voltage it calls full. Let it find this driver as
its supplier, and hear from it.

Name the gauge here rather than give it power-supplies in the tree. That
would keep the gauge from probing until this module loads, late in the
boot, and the gauge has to work without a charger: this driver waits for
it before taking over charging, and the charging watchdog reads its
temperature.

---
 drivers/power/supply/mt6375-charger.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/mt6375-charger.c b/drivers/power/supply/mt6375-charger.c
index 5fae6db..f2e7554 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/mt6375-charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/mt6375-charger.c
@@ -1865,6 +1865,9 @@ static int mt6375_chg_init_control(struct mt6375_chg *chg)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/* The gauge reports the status of the battery, and cannot see a charge end */
+static char *mt6375_chg_supplied_to[] = { "mm8013" };
+
 static int mt6375_chg_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
 	struct device *dev = &pdev->dev;
@@ -1913,6 +1916,8 @@ static int mt6375_chg_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	psy_cfg.drv_data = chg;
 	psy_cfg.fwnode = dev_fwnode(dev);
+	psy_cfg.supplied_to = mt6375_chg_supplied_to;
+	psy_cfg.num_supplicants = ARRAY_SIZE(mt6375_chg_supplied_to);
 	chg->psy = devm_power_supply_register(dev, &mt6375_chg_psy_desc,
 					      &psy_cfg);
 	if (IS_ERR(chg->psy))
